    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10674" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίφρᾰσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιφράζω</span>)
		Rhet. and Gramm., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>antiphrasis,</i> i.e. the use of words of good sense in place
			of those of a contrary sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὐμενίδες</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐρινύες,
				πόντος εὔξεινος</span> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄξεινος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.90b
			</span></i>; or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἄρα . . γήθησεν</span>
			for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλυπήθη,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Trypho
				<u>Trop.</u>
				2.15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ἀντίφρασιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Corn.
					<u>ND</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			, Erot.
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσήμοις</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Herm.
				<u>in Phdr.</u>
				p.176A.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Chr.</u>
				87
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>expression by means of negation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Anon.
				<u>Fig.</u>
				p.212S.
			</span></i>
		</div>
